# Environment "metricx": MetricX-24 quality estimation (preregistration.qmd, Outcome-neutral quality checks;
# supplementary.qmd S3), run from google-research/metricx at the commit pinned in config/resources.lock.json.
#
# The official pins, requirements.txt of google-research/metricx at commit fc4978eb (12 December 2024):
transformers[torch]==4.30.2
sentencepiece==0.1.99
datasets==2.13.1
# Left out: git+https://github.com/google-research/mt-metrics-eval, which serves meta-evaluation only;
# metricx24/predict.py and metricx24/models.py import datasets, torch and transformers, not mt_metrics_eval.
# A git dependency also cannot be hash-locked.
#
# Everything else upstream leaves open (torch, accelerate, pyarrow, fsspec, pandas) is resolved from PyPI as
# of that commit's date (uv pip compile --exclude-newer 2024-12-13T00:00:00Z; envs/README.md), so that the
# 2023 pins meet the releases a fresh install met when MetricX-24 was published, not 2026 releases that
# removed APIs they call. torch then resolves to its PyPI build with CUDA 12 libraries, which the L40S
# nodes' driver (580.65.06, recorded by the presub job logs) supports.
#
# Python 3.11 (ARC module Python/3.11.5-GCCcore-13.2.0): sentencepiece 0.1.99 and tokenizers 0.13.x, which
# transformers 4.30.2 requires, publish no CPython 3.12 wheels.
#
# A precaution, not an upstream pin: numpy 2.0 (June 2024) came a year after transformers 4.30.2 and
# datasets 2.13.1, so both predate its API changes.
numpy<2
# The converted MetricX weights are safetensors shards (jobs/arc/staging.py); transformers 4.30.2 reads them
# with this package.
safetensors
# Not upstream pins, but without them predict.py does not run (reproduced on 3 November 2026 with the lock's
# own versions on Python 3.11.5, tests/gpu/test_reference_gpu.py): transformers 4.30.2 converts mt5-xl's
# spiece.model with its T5Converter, which requires protobuf and whose generated module fails under protobuf 4
# and later ("Descriptors cannot be created directly"); and datasets 2.13.1 with fsspec 2024.10.0 stops with
# "Loading a dataset cached in a LocalFileSystem is not supported".
protobuf==3.20.3
fsspec[http]==2023.6.0
# The intract_features package is not installed here (envs/build_envs.sh): it needs Python 3.12 or later.
